{I left Charterhouse in December 1967, with a place at University College
Oxford in October 1968. From January to July 1968 I worked at the Phoenix
Assurance Company in the pensions department. I joined Wimbledon Chess Club at
the same time. So this season in 1968 was my first experience of proper chess
club matches.} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 g6 5. c4 b6 6. Nc3 Bg7 7.
Be3 Nf6 8. f3 e5 9. Ndb5 Bd7 10. Nxd6+ Kf8 11. c5 Qc7 12. Ndb5 Bxb5 13. Nxb5
Qc6 14. cxb6 axb6 15. Rc1 Qb7 16. Nc7 Ke7 17. Nxa8 Qxa8 18. Bxb6 Nbd7 19. Rc7
Qb8 20. Bc5+ Ke8 21. Bd6 Bf8 22. Rxd7 Bxd6 23. Rxd6 {and Black resigned - not
before time!} 1-0

