{A win against the British champion, even if only in a simul, is worth
celebrating. I played him 10 years later on top board for Surrey v Essex and
we agreed a short draw.} 1. c4 Nf6 2. Nc3 e6 3. e4 d5 4. cxd5 ({The main line
of the Mikenas system is} 4. e5 d4 (4... Ne4 {is an interesting line, which
Houdini seems to like} 5. Nxe4 dxe4 6. Qg4 Na6 7. Qxe4 Bd7 8. d4 Bc6 9. Qe3 Nb4
10. Kd2 Qd7 11. a3 Na6 {Vaznonis,V (2356)-Setkauskas,V (2186)/Plunge op 29th
2009 (7)/1-0}) 5. exf6 dxc3 6. bxc3 Qxf6 7. d4 e5 8. Nf3 exd4 9. Bg5 Qe6+ 10.
Be2 Be7 {Aronian,L (2807)-Kramnik,V (2791)/Moscow Botvinnik Memorial rapid
2011 (6)/1-0 but white has a healthy plus score in it e.g.}) 4... exd5 5. e5
Ne4 6. Nf3 Bc5 7. d4 Bb4 8. Qb3 c5 9. Be2 (9. Bb5+ $142 Nc6 10. O-O O-O 11.
dxc5 Bxc3 12. bxc3 Nxc5 13. Qc2 {which Houdini thinks is slightly better for
white}) 9... Nc6 10. O-O cxd4 (10... c4 11. Qc2 Bf5 12. Nxe4 Bxe4 13. Qd1 O-O {
may be stronger}) 11. Nb5 Bc5 12. Qd1 (12. Qxd5 $142 $1 {but after} Qxd5 13.
Nc7+ Kf8 14. Nxd5 Bf5 {Black is doing fine}) 12... Qb6 13. Bd3 Bg4 14. Bf4 a6 (
14... O-O $142) ({Rybka wants to play} 14... g5 $5 15. Bg3 O-O 16. a4 a6 17. a5
Nxa5 18. Nbxd4 Rac8) 15. Nd6+ Bxd6 16. exd6 O-O 17. h3 Bh5 18. Re1 Rfd8 (18...
Qxb2 19. Bxe4 dxe4 20. Rxe4 Bxf3 21. gxf3) 19. Bxe4 dxe4 20. Rxe4 d3 21. Re1
Nd4 22. g4 Ne2+ 23. Rxe2 dxe2 24. Qxe2 Bg6 25. Re1 Qb4 26. Bg3 h5 27. Ne5 Rxd6
28. gxh5 $2 Bxh5 29. Qf1 Qxe1 {simplest, exchanging pieces into a won ending.}
30. Qxe1 Rd1 31. Qxd1 Bxd1 32. Nc4 Rc8 33. b3 b5 34. Ne3 Bf3 35. Kh2 Rc1 36.
Be5 f6 37. Bd4 b4 38. Kg3 Be4 39. Kf4 Bb1 40. Nd5 Rd1 0-1

