1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Bxc6 {I needed a win,
John a draw to get in the prizes. I played this, "au Lasker v Capablanca" to
avoid the Marshall Gambit and get a position where he might be tempted just to
try swapping off pieces into a lost endgame.} dxc6 7. Qe1 Nd7 8. d4 exd4 9.
Nxd4 O-O 10. Be3 Nc5 11. f3 f5 12. exf5 Bxf5 13. Nxf5 Rxf5 14. Nc3 Qf8 15. Rd1
Re8 16. Qe2 Bd6 17. Qc4+ Qf7 18. Qxf7+ Rxf7 19. Bxc5 Bxc5+ 20. Kh1 Re3 21. Ne4
Bd6 22. Rfe1 Rxe1+ 23. Rxe1 b6 24. Rd1 Rd7 25. g3 Rd8 26. Kg2 Be7 27. Rxd8+
Bxd8 28. f4 Kf7 29. Kf3 Ke6 30. Nc3 (30. Nf2 Kd5 31. Ng4 g6 32. c3 c5 33. Ne3+
Ke6 34. Ke4 $14) 30... b5 31. Ke4 c5 32. g4 h6 33. Nd5 c6 34. Ne3 $2 (34. f5+
$142 Kd6 35. Nf4 Bf6 36. b3 $16) 34... c4 35. Nf5 Bf6 36. c3 c5 37. h4 b4 38.
cxb4 cxb4 39. Nd4+ Kd6 $4 (39... Kf7 40. g5 Be7 41. Nf3 c3 42. bxc3 bxc3 43.
Ne5+ Ke6 44. f5+ Kd6 45. Nf7+ Kd7 46. Kd3 hxg5 47. hxg5 Ke8 48. g6 Bf6 $11) 40.
g5 {We were now into a ten minute play-off.} hxg5 41. hxg5 Bxd4 42. Kxd4 Ke6
43. Kxc4 Kf5 44. Kxb4 Kxf4 45. g6 Kf5 46. Ka5 Kxg6 47. Kxa6 Kf5 48. b4 $2 ({
Missing a clever win, which I only found on the way home after the game. I
showed it to John Nunn a week later and he subsequently included it in his
book Tactical Chess Endings.} 48. Kb5 $1 g5 49. Kc4 Ke4 (49... g4 50. Kd3 Kf4
51. a4 Kf3 52. a5 g3 53. a6 g2 54. a7 g1=Q 55. a8=Q+ Kf4 56. Qe4+ Kg5 57. Qe3+
$18) 50. a4 g4 51. a5 g3 52. a6 g2 53. a7 g1=Q 54. a8=Q+ Kf4 55. Qf8+ Ke4 56.
Qe7+ Kf4 57. Qd6+ Ke4 58. Qd5+ Kf4 59. Qd4+ $18) 48... g5 49. b5 g4 50. b6 g3
51. b7 g2 52. b8=Q g1=Q 53. a4 Qd4 54. a5 Kg4 {Agreed drawn} 1/2-1/2

