1. f4 e5 2. fxe5 d6 3. exd6 Bxd6 4. Nf3 g5 5. d4 (5. g3 {Wegemund,O-Kruger,P/
DSB-18.Kongress-C 1912/1-0 is an old line which has been resurrected in the
computer age. After} g4 6. Nh4 Ne7 7. d4 Ng6 8. Nxg6 hxg6 9. Qd3 Nc6 10. c3 {
Rendle,T (2370)-Kotronias,V (2585)/Gibraltar Masters 2005 (1)/ 0-1 white has a
preponderance of pawns in the centre, which carry the hope of a long term
advantage. This line has been played several times by Tom Rendle. Although he
lost to his strongest opponent, that was not the fault of the opening}) 5... g4
6. Ng5 f5 7. e4 h6 8. e5 Be7 9. Nh3 gxh3 10. Qh5+ Kf8 11. Bc4 Rh7 12. Bxg8 ({If
} 12. Qg6 Rg7 13. Bxh6 Bb4+ 14. Ke2 Nxh6 15. Qxh6 Qg5 $17 {Lansing-Geula,F/
Michigan op 1973/0-1}) 12... Kxg8 13. c3 Bg5 14. Nd2 hxg2 15. Rg1 Bd7 (15...
Nc6 $142 16. Rxg2 Kh8 17. Nf3 Bxc1 18. Rxc1 Be6 $19) 16. Rxg2 Rg7 17. Nf3 Bxc1
$2 (17... Be8 18. Qh3 f4 19. Bxf4 Bxf4 20. Rxg7+ Kxg7 21. Qg4+ Bg5 22. h4 Qd5
23. hxg5 h5 $17) 18. Rxg7+ Kxg7 19. Rxc1 Qe8 20. Qh4 Nc6 $4 ({Black must play} 
20... a5 {to swing his rook over to the king's side} 21. Kf2 Ra6 22. Rg1+ Rg6)
21. Kf2 Qf8 22. Rg1+ Kh7 $4 (22... Kf7 23. Qh5+ Ke7 24. d5 Na5 25. e6 Bb5 26.
Qh4+ Ke8 27. e7 Qh8 28. Rg6 {is winning as well}) 23. Ng5+ Kh8 24. e6 Be8 25.
Nf7+ $4 (25. e7 $1 Nxe7 26. Ne6 $18) 25... Bxf7 26. exf7 $2 (26. Qf6+ Kh7 27.
exf7 Ne7 {transposes to the game, but}) 26... Ne7 $2 ({I should have played} 
26... Qd6 27. Re1 Rf8 28. d5 Nd8 29. Re6 $1 Qc5+ 30. Kf1 Nxf7 31. Rxh6+ {draws}
) 27. Qf6+ Kh7 28. Re1 Ng6 29. Qxf5 $4 (29. Re6 Nh8 30. Qe5 Nxf7 31. Qxf5+ Kh8
32. Rf6 Kg8 33. Qg4+ Kh8 34. Qg6 $18) 29... Kg7 30. Kf3 Nh4+ 0-1

