1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. dxe5 dxe5 8. O-O
(8. Qxd8 Rxd8 9. Bg5 Re8 10. Nd5 Nxd5 11. cxd5 c6 12. Bc4 {is the usual line,
generally for no better than a draw e.g. Flohr,S-Bronstein,D/Candidates
Tournament 1950 (4)/1/2-1/2}) 8... c6 9. Qc2 Nbd7 (9... Qc7 10. b3 Nbd7 11. Ba3
Re8 12. Rad1 Bf8 {would be similar to the game e.g. Napolitano,M-Palmiotto,F/
ITA-ch 19th Reggio Emilia 1957 (2)/1-0}) 10. b3 Re8 11. Rd1 Qc7 12. Ba3 Nf8 $4
(12... Bf8 {was of course correct, but I'd just gone to sleep.} 13. Bxf8 Nxf8
14. c5 Bg4 15. Nd2 Ne6 16. Bxg4 Nxg4 17. b4 {Yapici,K (1905) -Severcan,S (2006)
/ch-TUR Kemer-Antalya TUR 2011 (3)/0-1}) 13. Bd6 Qa5 14. b4 {and white won in
22 moves} 1-0

