{First game of the 1972-3 season. Grade 173 per CHESS, although my
calculations make it 186!} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Bb5+ {
a line suggested to me by C W Hallows} Bd7 6. c4 Nc6 7. Bxc6 (7. Nc3 g6 8. f3 {
Boey,J (2277)-Chernikov,O (2422)/Wch Seniors 16th 2006 (4)/1-0 resembles a
Maroczy bind dragon with the white bishop outside the pawns}) 7... Bxc6 8. Nxc6
bxc6 9. Nc3 g6 10. Be3 Bg7 11. f3 Qa5 12. Qa4 (12. Qd2 $143 Qb4 13. Rc1 Nd7 14.
O-O a5) 12... Qxa4 13. Nxa4 O-O 14. Kf2 Rfb8 15. Rac1 Nd7 16. b3 Ne5 17. Rhd1
c5 18. h3 Rb7 19. Rd2 Nc6 20. Rcd1 (20. f4 $142 Nd4 21. e5 Rc8 22. g4 dxe5 23.
fxe5 Bxe5 24. Nxc5 Rxc5 25. Bxd4 Bxd4+ 26. Rxd4 $14) 20... Nd4 21. f4 e5 22.
Bxd4 cxd4 23. fxe5 dxe5 24. g4 f5 {Black was typically short of time now} 25.
gxf5 gxf5 26. exf5 Rf7 27. Nc5 Rxf5+ 28. Kg2 Raf8 29. Re2 Bh6 30. Nd7 R8f7 $4 (
30... Rg5+ 31. Kh2 Rff5 $15) 31. Nxe5 $16 {Adjudicated a win for white.} 1-0

