(8. Nf3 Bb4 9. Bd3 $14 {is stronger.}) 8... Bb4 9. Nf3 c5 $146 10. a3 cxd4 11.
axb4 dxe3 12. Qxd8+ ({The Cambridge team had analysed a line going} 12. Nb5 O-O
(12... Nc6 13. Nd6+ Kf8 {Mirzoeva,E (2010)-Driamin,D (2225)/Moscow-ch 1996 (6)/
0-1} 14. Be2) 13. Qxd8 Rxd8 14. Nc7 Nc6 15. Nxa8 Nxb4 16. Nxb6 Nc2+ 17. Ke2
Nxa1 18. Na4 Nc2 {Rybka reckons} 19. Nc5 b5 20. Nb7 Rd7 21. Nd6 bxc4 {is equal.
}) 12... Kxd8 13. O-O-O+ $2 ({Much better is} 13. Nd1 Na6 14. b5 Nb4 15. Nxe3 {
with a roughly equal position.}) ({The database has three games with} 13. c5
N6d7 14. Bb5 Ke7 {Laszlo,I (2182)-Panchenko,A (2402)/ Nyiregyhaza op 2003 (2)/
1/2-1/2 e.g.}) 13... Ke7 14. c5 N6d7 15. Bd3 Bxd3 16. Rxd3 a5 17. b5 Nxc5 18.
Rxe3 Nbd7 19. Rd1 Nb6 20. Kc2 Rhd8 21. Ree1 h6 22. b3 Rac8 23. Rxd8 Rxd8 24.
Ra1 Rc8 25. Nd2 a4 26. b4 Ncd7 27. Kb2 Nxe5 28. Nxa4 Nd5 29. Nc5 {Although
objectively this might not be best, at least white ends up with a passed pawn
and some threats.} Nxb4 30. Nxb7 Rc2+ 31. Kb3 Rxd2 32. Kxb4 Rxg2 33. Nc5 Rxh2
34. b6 Rb2+ 35. Nb3 Kd6 $6 ({It seems better to give up knight for white's
remaining pawn by} 35... Nc6+ 36. Kc3 Rf2 $19 {than give up the exchange.}) 36.
Kc3 Rxb3+ ({And now} 36... Rg2 37. Na5 Rg3+ 38. Kc2 Rg4 (38... Nc6 39. Rd1+ Kc5
40. b7 Nb4+ 41. Kb2) 39. Rd1+ Kc5 40. b7 Rb4 41. Rd8 Nc6 42. Nxc6 (42. Rc8 Kd5
43. Rxc6 Rxb7 44. Nxb7 Kxc6 45. Nd8+ Kd5 46. Nxf7 {is a draw per Nalimov!})
42... Rxb7 {,again giving up a piece rather than the exchange, may be better.})
37. Kxb3 Kc6 ({If} 37... Nd7 38. Ra7 {may be best} (38. Kb4 Nxb6 39. Ra6 Kc6
40. Ka5 g5 41. Rxb6+ Kc5 {is apparently a black win per 7-piece Nalimov.})
38... g5 (38... f6 39. b7 Nb8) 39. b7 Nb8 40. Ra1) 38. Ra5 Nd7 39. Ra7 Nc5+ 40.
Kc3 Nb7 41. Ra8 Kxb6 ({Houdini prefers} 41... Nd6 $1 42. Rd8 g5 43. Kd4 g4 44.
Ke5 Nf5) 42. Rg8 g6 {Now white's king can infiltrate the black pawns.} (42...
g5 {should win} 43. Kd4 (43. Rh8 Kc5 44. Rxh6 g4 45. Kd3 Kd5 46. Rf6 Nd6 47.
Ke2 Ke5 48. Rh6 f5) 43... Nd6 44. Ke5 Kc6 45. Rh8 Nf5) 43. Kd4 Kc6 (43... Nd6
44. Ke5 Kc5 45. Rf8 g5 46. Rd8 Nc4+ 47. Kf6 e5 48. Kf5 f6 49. Rd7) 44. Ke5 h5
45. Kf6 Nd6 46. Rh8 Kc5 ({If} 46... Kd5 47. Ra8 h4 48. Ra5+ Kd4 49. Ra4+ Nc4
50. Kxf7 g5 51. Kf6 g4 52. Kg5 g3 53. Kxh4 g2 54. Ra1 $11) 47. Rd8 h4 48. Rh8
e5 (48... Kd5 49. Rxh4 e5 50. Rh1 e4 51. Rd1+ Kc5 52. Ke5 e3 53. Rc1+ Nc4+ 54.
Ke4 e2 55. Re1 Nd6+ 56. Kf4) 49. Kxe5 g5 50. Rd8 Nb5 (50... f6+ 51. Kxf6 g4 52.
Kg5 g3 53. Kxh4) 51. Rc8+ 1/2-1/2

