1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. O-O Nf6 5. d4 Bxd4 6. Nxd4 Nxd4 7. Bg5 d6 8.
f4 Qe7 9. Nc3 c6 10. a4 $146 ({Estrin on p131 recommends} 10. fxe5 dxe5 11. Rf2
Be6 12. Bd3 h6 13. Bxf6 gxf6 {Freiman,S-Bernstein,O/RUS-ch Vilnius 1912 (1)/0-1
} 14. Qf1 O-O-O 15. Rxf6 {"with a complicated position in which both sides
have chances." My idea is designed to restrict black's queen's side.}) 10...
Be6 11. Bd3 h6 12. Bxf6 Qxf6 13. f5 Bc8 14. Nb1 Qg5 15. Kh1 c5 16. Bc4 O-O 17.
c3 Bxf5 18. cxd4 Bxe4 19. Qe2 Bxb1 20. Raxb1 cxd4 21. Qe4 Qe7 22. Rf3 Rac8 23.
b3 Rc7 24. Rbf1 Kh8 25. h4 Qd8 26. h5 Rxc4 ({Desperation but how else to stop
the threat of mate?} 26... Qg5 27. Bd3 g6 (27... Qxh5+ 28. Rh3) 28. hxg6 f6 29.
Qd5 {is awful for black}) 27. bxc4 Qc7 28. Qd5 f6 29. Rb1 (29. Rb1 {and black
resigned.} b6 30. a5 Rb8 31. Rfb3 {forces a queen's side breakthrough.}) 1-0

