1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. c3 dxc3 5. Nxc3 Bb4 6. Bc4 d6 7. O-O Bxc3 8.
bxc3 Nf6 9. e5 Nxe5 10. Nxe5 dxe5 11. Qb3 Qe7 12. Ba3 c5 13. Bb5+ Kf8 ({
The alternative, which scores slightly better, is} 13... Bd7 14. Bxd7+ Qxd7 15.
Bxc5 Ne4 16. Ba3 Nd2 17. Qb4 O-O-O {Ljubojevic,L-Stupica,J/ YUG-ch 24th Novi
Travnik 1969 (13)/1/2-1/2}) 14. f4 e4 15. f5 b6 16. Bc6 Rb8 17. c4 $6 (17. Rad1
Bb7 18. Bxb7 {Perez Garcia,H (2205)-Plasman,H (2160)/ NED-ch sf Enschede 1998 
(9)/1-0} Rxb7 $17) 17... Bb7 (17... Qd6 $142 18. Bd5 Bb7) 18. Bxb7 Rxb7 19. Bb2
h5 20. Rae1 h4 (20... Rd7 $142 21. Rf4 Kg8 22. Bxf6 Qxf6 23. Rfxe4 Qxf5 $17)
21. Rf4 Rh6 22. Bxf6 Qxf6 23. Rfxe4 Kg8 24. Re8+ Kh7 25. Qf3 Rd7 {we were both
short of time by now} 26. Qa8 ({Rybka reckons that it's better to play} 26. h3
{first} Qg5 27. Qa8 Qxf5 28. Rh8+ Kg6 29. Qc6+ Kg5 30. Rxh6 gxh6 {Rybka still
assesses this as better for black, but his king is very exposed, so in
practice it's not easy}) 26... Qxf5 27. Rh8+ Kg6 28. Qc6+ f6 29. Rf8 Rh5 30.
Rf1 Qd3 (30... Qd3 {agreed drawn on account of} 31. R1xf6+ Kh7 32. Rf1 h3 33.
Qe6 Qd4+ 34. R1f2 Qd1+ ({but Rybka reckons that} 34... Re7 {!} 35. Qxe7 Re5 36.
Qxe5 Qxe5 37. R8f3 Qa1+ 38. Rf1 Qd4+ 39. R1f2 Qxc4 40. Rxh3+ Kg8 {is winning
for black})) 1/2-1/2

