1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Ba5 6. b4 cxd4 7. Qg4 Ne7 8. Nb5
Bc7 9. Qxg7 Rg8 10. Qxh7 a6 11. Nxc7+ Qxc7 12. Ne2 Bd7 13. f4 a5 14. bxa5 Qxa5+
15. Bd2 Qb6 16. Qd3 $6 ({This frees up the knight on e7.} 16. Ng3 $142 {
Levy,D (2350)-Nilsson,Z/Lugano ol (Men) fin-B 1968 (12)/0-1} Qb2 17. Rc1 Bb5
18. Bxb5+ Qxb5 19. f5 $16 {according to Rybka.}) 16... Nf5 17. Qb3 Qc7 $6 {
Keeping the position complicated. We had both taken about an hour up to here,
but I started to fall behind on the clock.} 18. Ng3 Nxg3 19. hxg3 Na6 20. Bxa6
bxa6 21. Rb1 Rc8 22. Qb6 $6 Qxc2 23. Rc1 Qe4+ $2 24. Kf2 Rd8 25. Qxa6 {I spent
a priceless 8 minutes on this move, leaving me only a couple to get to move 30.
} Rb8 26. Kg1 d3 27. Qa7 Rb2 $6 {Objectively a huge blunder! But played to
make me lose on time, which I obligingly did.} (27... Rd8 28. Rh4 {and white
still has the advantage.}) (27... Rb2 28. Qa8+ Ke7 29. Qxg8 Rxd2 30. Qg5+ {
and mates.}) 0-1

