1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nd4 4. Ba4 Nxf3+ 5. Qxf3 Bc5 6. Qg3 Qf6 7. d3 Ne7 8.
O-O h6 9. Be3 Bxe3 ({There are only three games on the database with this line,
all continuing} 9... Bb6 {I (and Rybka!) think my move is better. Nigel had
another game with this line in the British Championships 4 years later, which
he won:} 10. c4 (10. Nc3 {Schallopp, E-Flechsig,E/Leipzig 1877 (2)/1-0}) 10...
Bxe3 11. fxe3 Qg5 12. Qxg5 hxg5 13. Nc3 {Povah,N (2325)-Horner,J (2390)/BCF-ch
Chester 1979 (4)/1-0}) 10. fxe3 Qg5 11. Qf2 O-O 12. Bb3 Qg6 (12... Qh5 {
stops white's queen getting to h4.}) 13. Nc3 c6 14. Qh4 Qg5 15. Qxg5 hxg5 16.
Rf2 (16. Rf3 $142 {because} d6 (16... g4 $142 17. Rf2 Ng6 18. Raf1 Nh8 19. d4
d6 {although it's somewhat uncomfortable for black.}) 17. Raf1 Be6 18. Bxe6
fxe6 19. Rg3 {wins a pawn}) 16... d6 17. Raf1 Be6 18. Bxe6 fxe6 19. Rf3 {
one tempo too late!} Rxf3 20. Rxf3 Kh7 21. Rg3 Kh6 22. Nb1 Ng8 23. Nd2 Nf6 24.
Nf3 g4 25. Nd2 Rf8 1/2-1/2

