1. Nf3 Nf6 2. b3 g6 3. Bb2 Bg7 4. c4 O-O 5. g3 d6 6. Bg2 e5 7. O-O Nbd7 ({
I used to put the QN on d7 regularly, whereas} 7... Nc6 {is probably better.})
8. d3 Nh5 9. e4 Nc5 10. b4 Ne6 11. Nh4 a5 12. a3 Bd7 (12... Nhf4 $1 {exhanging
off white's KB, gives black some advantage, e.g.} 13. Nf3 Nxg2 14. Kxg2 f5 15.
Nc3 f4 16. h3 axb4 17. axb4 Rxa1 18. Bxa1 Nd4 $15) 13. Nf5 gxf5 14. Qxh5 f4 15.
Nd2 Qf6 16. Bh3 Ba4 (16... Bh6 17. Qe2 (17. Nf3 Ng7 $19) 17... Nd4 18. Qh5 Bxh3
19. Qxh3 fxg3 20. fxg3 Be3+ 21. Kg2 Qg6 22. Nf3 Nc2 $15) 17. Nf3 axb4 18. axb4
Qh6 19. Qxh6 Bxh6 20. Ra3 Bc2 21. Rfa1 Rxa3 22. Rxa3 Bd1 23. Bg2 Rb8 24. Nh4
fxg3 25. hxg3 Bd2 26. Bc3 Bxc3 27. Rxc3 Ra8 28. Nf5 Ra1 29. Kh2 Nd4 ({Best to
keep the knight on e6 to guard c5.} 29... Ra2 30. Kg1 Be2 31. Bf1 Ra1 32. Ne3
Rb1 33. b5 Nc5 34. Kg2 Bxf1+ 35. Nxf1 Rd1 $15) 30. Ne3 Be2 31. c5 Nb5 (31...
Ra2 32. cxd6 cxd6 33. Kg1 Ra1+ 34. Kh2 Rb1 35. Rc8+ Kg7 36. Rd8 $11) 32. cxd6
$1 Nxc3 33. dxc7 Ra8 34. Bh3 Bxd3 (34... Bxd3 {Agreed drawn in the light of}
35. f3 b5 36. c8=Q+ Rxc8 37. Bxc8 Na2 38. Ng4 {preserving material equality.})
1/2-1/2

