1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Nf6 3. c4 c6 4. d4 cxd5 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. Bg5 Qa5 7. Qd2 ({
The most popular line on the database, which I have played twice without
eventual success, is} 7. Bxf6 exf6 8. cxd5 Bb4 9. Qd2 Bxc3 10. bxc3 Qxd5 11.
Nf3 O-O 12. Be2 Na5 {was Murray Chandler's later improvement in Shamkovich,L 
(2500)-Chandler,M (2530)/Lloyds Bank op 05th 1981 (3)/1/2-1/2} (12... Bf5 13.
O-O Na5 ({An improvement on} 13... b5 14. a4 a6 15. Qa2 {Emerson,R-Wade,R 
(2410)/London League [2]/0-1 in a game where I got a winning advantage and
then mucked it up}) 14. Qb2 {Emerson,R-Chandler,M (2282)/ Surrey Open (4)/0-1
and we reached a drawn ending which I again managed to muck up})) 7... dxc4 ({
In ECO Botvinnik gives} 7... e5 8. Bxf6 gxf6 9. Nxd5 Qxd2+ 10. Kxd2 Bh6+ 11.
Kc3 ({I prefer} 11. f4 O-O 12. Nf3 $14 {Mukharev,I (2256)-Khabibullin,A/
RUS-Cup Tomsk 1999 (2)/1-0}) 11... exd4+ 12. Kb3 O-O {Fuchs,R-Packroff,H/
DDR-ch 17th Weimar 1968 (16)/1-0} 13. Bd3 {with a slight advantage to white,
whereas Rybka assesses it as slighly better for black!}) 8. d5 ({Botvinnik and
Rybka both prefer} 8. Bxc4 {and then Rybka suggests} Bg4 (8... e5 9. d5 Nd4 10.
f4 {was Keres v Czerniak 1939}) 9. h3 Bh5 10. Nge2 e6 $11) 8... Ne5 9. Qd4 Nd3+
10. Bxd3 cxd3 11. Nf3 Bf5 12. O-O h6 13. Bh4 g5 ({Rybka recommends} 13... Rd8
14. Bxf6 gxf6 15. Rfe1 Rg8 16. Qxf6 Rxd5 $1 17. Nxd5 Qxd5 18. Re3 e6 {which it
assesses as equal.}) 14. Rfe1 Bg7 15. Qe5 O-O 16. Qxf5 gxh4 17. Qxd3 Rad8 18.
Rad1 e6 19. d6 h3 20. Re5 Qb6 21. gxh3 Nd5 (21... Nd7 $142 22. Rb5 Qc6 23. Rh5
Rc8 $14) 22. Nxd5 exd5 23. Rxd5 Qxb2 24. Nd4 ({Time trouble. better is} 24. Rb1
Qxa2 25. Rxb7 a5 26. d7 {with a winning advantage}) (24. Rh5 Qxa2 25. Ng5 f5
26. Rd2 Qa1+ 27. Rd1 $11) (24. a3 Rd7 25. Nh4 Kh8 26. Nf5 Rg8 27. Kf1) 24...
Bxd4 25. Qxd4 Qxd4 26. R1xd4 Rd7 27. Kg2 f5 $2 28. Rc4 $2 ({Again, better is} 
28. Kf3 Rf6 29. Kf4 Kg7 30. h4 Kg6 (30... Rg6 31. Kxf5 Rf6+ 32. Ke5 Rxf2 33.
Ke6 Rff7 34. Rf5) 31. Ke5 Kf7 32. h5 b6 33. f4 {and wait for black to run out
of pawn moves} a6 34. Rd2 b5 35. Rd1 {before playing} Re6+ ({or} 35... Kg7 36.
Rg1+ Kf7 37. Rg6) 36. Kxf5 Rf6+ 37. Ke4 Re6+ 38. Kf3 Kf6 39. a3 Kf7 40. f5)
28... Rf6 29. Rc7 $2 (29. Rcd4 $142 Kg7 30. Kf3 Re6 31. Kf4 Kg6 32. f3 Re2 33.
Re5 Rxa2 34. Re6+ Kg7 35. Kxf5) 29... Rdxd6 30. Rxd6 Rxd6 31. Rxb7 1/2-1/2

