{The first round, accelerated pairings - top against second quartile.} 1. e4 e5
2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. c3 dxc3 5. Nxc3 Bb4 6. Bc4 d6 7. O-O Bxc3 8. bxc3 Bg4
{Brian Denman had shown me the Karaklajic game a few months before. I'm not
sure that Hindle was aware of it. So different from today's databases!} 9. Qb3
Bxf3 10. Bxf7+ Kf8 11. Bxg8 Rxg8 12. gxf3 Ne5 13. f4 Nf3+ 14. Kg2 Nh4+ 15. Kh1
Qd7 16. f5 (16. c4 {was a subsequent improvement}) ({but Rybka thinks that} 16.
f3 Qh3 ({or} 16... Qc6 17. Bd2 Re8 18. Be1 Nxf3 19. Rxf3 Rxe4 20. Kg1 g6 21.
Rb1 b6) 17. Rf2 {is even stronger}) (16. Rg1 Qc6 17. Re1 Re8 18. Qc2 {and now
Houdini suggests} Ke7 {getting the black king over to the queen's side before
assaulting white's king.}) (16. Qd1 Qh3 17. Rg1 Nf3 18. Rg2 Re8) 16... Qc6 17.
f3 Re8 18. Qc2 g5 19. Rb1 ({So far we were following Ciocaltea,V-Karaklajic,N/
Smederevska Palanka 1971/0-1:} 19. fxg6 Nxg6 20. Bh6+ Ke7) 19... b6 ({A waste
of time.} 19... g4 $142) 20. Rb4 g4 21. Bh6+ Ke7 $2 22. f6+ $2 (22. fxg4 Rxg4
23. Qe2 Rgg8 24. Rc4 Qb7 25. f6+ Kf7 26. Qh5+ Ng6 27. Qd5+ Qxd5 28. Rxc7+ Ke6
29. exd5+ Kxd5 30. f7 $18) 22... Kf7 23. Qb3+ Re6 24. Rc4 Qb7 25. Qb5 $2 (25.
f4 $142 Nf5 26. Bg5 d5 27. Rc5 $1 Rxe4 28. Rxd5 Kg6 $15) 25... c5 26. Ra4 Nxf3
27. Bg7 Ng5 (27... Rxe4 $142 28. Qa6 Qxa6 29. Rxa6 Re2 30. Rxf3 gxf3 31. Kg1
Rg2+ 32. Kf1 Ra8 $19) 28. Qa6 Qxa6 29. Rxa6 Ra8 30. Rb1 d5 (30... Nxe4 31.
Rbxb6 axb6 32. Rxa8 Nxc3 33. Ra7+ Kg6 $19) 31. exd5 Re2 32. Bh6 Nf3 33. Bf4 h5
34. Rbxb6 $2 (34. Bc7 Rf2 35. Ra4 Kxf6 {is winning, but there's still work to
do.}) 34... axb6 35. Rxa8 h4 {Now white is in a mating net.} 36. Bd6 h3 37.
Rf8+ Kg6 38. Bg3 Rg2 39. Rg8+ Kf5 0-1

