{Not a very distinguished game, but any win against an IM is worth celebrating!
} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 e6 5. Nc3 Qc7 6. Be3 a6 7. Bd3 Nf6 8.
O-O Bd6 9. h3 Bf4 10. Bxf4 Qxf4 11. Nde2 Qc7 12. f4 d6 13. Kh1 b5 14. Bxb5 $5 (
{Approved by Houdini!} 14. a3 {was played in Mamedov,N (2446)-Klimov,S (2509)/
Moscow Aeroflot op-B 2005 (2)/1-0 after which Black should just play} O-O {
. Instead Klimov allowed white to sac on b5.}) 14... axb5 15. Nxb5 Qe7 $6 ({
Houdini thinks that best is the unnatural looking} 15... Qd7 16. Nxd6+ Ke7 17.
e5 Ne8 18. Qe1 Nxd6 19. Rd1 Ba6 20. exd6+ Kf8) 16. Nxd6+ Kf8 17. e5 Ne8 18. Nc3
Bb7 19. Ncb5 Rd8 20. Qf3 Ba8 21. Qc3 g6 ({Houdini thinks that} 21... Na7 22.
Nxa7 Qxa7 23. Rad1 Kg8 {as equal}) 22. b4 $14 Ng7 23. a4 Nf5 24. Nxf5 $2 {
Better to ignore the knight and push on with the queen's side pawns.} gxf5 25.
Nd6 Rg8 26. Rf3 Rg6 $2 (26... Nd4 $1) 27. Kh2 Nxb4 $1 28. Qxb4 Bxf3 29. gxf3
Kg8 30. Qe1 Qc7 31. c4 Rb8 $2 (31... Qc5 32. Rd1 Ra8 33. Rd2 Rxa4 $19) 32. Qf2
Qc6 33. Ra2 Kg7 34. Qe3 Rb4 35. Rg2 $2 ({Houdini reckons that best is} 35. a5)
35... Rxg2+ 36. Kxg2 Rb2+ 37. Kg3 Qxa4 38. Kh4 Qc2 39. Ne8+ Kg6 40. Qg1+ Qg2
41. Qxg2+ Rxg2 42. Nd6 Rc2 43. Kg3 h6 44. Kh4 Kg7 45. Ne8+ Kf8 46. Nd6 Rc3 47.
Kg3 Ke7 48. Nc8+ Kd7 49. Nd6 f6 50. Nf7 fxe5 $2 (50... Ke7 51. Nd6 h5 52. h4
Kd7 53. Nf7 fxe5 54. Nxe5+ Kd6 55. Kf2 Kc5 {wins. If} 56. Ke2 Rc2+ 57. Kd3 Rh2
58. Ng6 Rh3) 51. fxe5 $4 (51. Nxe5+ $17 {The difference is that white can win
black's h-pawn.}) 51... h5 52. Nd6 h4+ 53. Kxh4 Rxf3 54. c5 Re3 55. Nf7 Ke7 56.
Nh8 Kf8 57. Ng6+ Kf7 0-1

