better percentage in the database than} 9... cxd4 10. Nxd4 Nxd4 11. Bxd4 {
Kinnmark,O (2385)-Paoli,E (2270)/Eksjo 03rd 1975 (3)/1/2-1/2 e.g.}) 10. c4 ({
White spent a further half an hour thinking about} 10. dxc5 {after which} Qxd1
11. Rxd1 Ng4 12. Bf4 Bxc5 13. Bg3 O-O {leaves white with a slight advantage,
because Black finds it difficult to develop his QB.}) 10... O-O 11. Nc3 cxd4
12. Nxd4 Qc7 13. Qe2 (13. Nxc6 Qxc6 {Kinnmark,O (2390)-Schneider,L (2365)/
SWE-ch Motala 1976/1/2-1/2}) 13... Bd7 14. Rac1 {By now white had less than 10
minutes for his next 20 moves.} Rac8 15. h3 Rfd8 16. Nxc6 Bxc6 17. Red1 Qa5 18.
Bd4 Rd7 19. Qe3 Qb4 (19... Qh5 {may be objectively better, but I was playing
on white's time shortage to complicate the game.}) 20. a3 Qxb2 21. Nd5 Qxa3 22.
Rd3 Qa5 $2 ({Dangerous, but} 22... Qd6 23. Nxf6+ gxf6 24. Bxf6 Qxd3 25. Bxd3
Bxf6 {simplifies too much}) 23. Nxf6+ $2 ({White was down to a minute to get
to move 35.} 23. Bb6 Nxd5 24. cxd5 Qb4 25. dxc6 Rxd3 26. Bxd3 Rxc6 27. Rxc6
bxc6 28. Qe4 {should win.}) 23... Bxf6 24. Bxf6 Rxd3 25. Bxd3 gxf6 26. Qh6 $2 (
26. c5 Rd8 27. Be4 Qd2 28. Qxd2 Rxd2 29. Bxc6 bxc6 30. Ra1 Rc2 31. Ra5 {
is best, but black has a big advantage.}) 26... Qg5 $1 27. Qxh7+ Kf8 28. g3
Qxc1+ 0-1

