1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. g4 a6 7. g5 Nfd7 8. Be3
Nc6 9. Rg1 Nde5 10. Be2 b5 11. f4 Nxd4 12. Qxd4 Nc6 13. Qd2 Qa5 ({The only
game on the database, which reached this position by transposition, went} 13...
Bb7 14. a3 {Damjanovic,M (2320)-Galic,K (2230)/ CRO-chT2 Medulin 1997/1-0}) 14.
Bf3 Bd7 15. Ne2 Qxd2+ 16. Bxd2 Be7 ({Rybka suggests,} 16... g6 17. O-O-O h6 18.
h4 hxg5 19. hxg5 Bg7 20. Be3 Ke7 {but still with a slight advantage to white.})
17. O-O-O O-O 18. Be3 Rac8 19. Nd4 Rfd8 20. Rg3 {draw agreed. A draw with the
many times British champion isn't bad, although I had a slight edge.} (20. Rg3
$14 {The game might proceed} Nxd4 21. Bxd4 Bc6 22. Bg2 Bb7 23. f5 d5 24. f6 Bd6
25. e5 Bc5 26. Bf1 {with a slight advantage to white. Black has difficulty
generating counterplay and is in danger of getting to an ending with a bad
white square bishop, although the position is fairly blocked.}) 1/2-1/2

