{New season with my grade back up to 201, published in CHESS September 1976.} 
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 6. d4 b5 7. Bb3 d5 8. dxe5
Be6 9. Qe2 Nc5 10. Rd1 Nxb3 11. axb3 Qc8 12. c3 (12. c4 $142 $1 dxc4 13. bxc4
Bxc4 14. Qe4 {as in Smyslov - Euwe 1948, where white won in 26 moves. although
Rybka reckons that} Nb4 15. Bg5 h6 16. Rd8+ Qxd8 17. Bxd8 Rxd8 {Petrosian,
T-Lilienthal,A/Moscow exh 1957/1-0} 18. Na3 {is equal!}) 12... Be7 13. b4 {
I thought this would create long term pressure against black's queen's side
pawns.} O-O 14. Be3 f6 15. exf6 Bxf6 16. Nbd2 Re8 17. Qd3 Ne7 18. Nd4 Bf5 19.
Nxf5 Qxf5 20. Nb3 Qxd3 21. Rxd3 Nf5 22. Kf1 $6 (22. Bd2 $142) 22... Nxe3+ 23.
fxe3 Re5 24. Nc5 Bg5 25. Rxa6 Rae8 26. Nd7 R5e7 27. Rxd5 Bxe3 28. g3 Rf7+ 29.
Kg2 Rf2+ 30. Kh3 Rxb2 31. Re5 $2 (31. Rxb5 Bg1 32. Re5 Rxh2+ 33. Kg4) 31...
Rxe5 32. Nxe5 h5 33. Rc6 g5 34. Rxc7 Bg1 35. Ng4 1/2-1/2

