1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e5 6. Ndb5 d6 7. Bg5 a6 8.
Na3 b5 9. Bxf6 gxf6 10. Nd5 f5 11. Bxb5 axb5 12. Nxb5 Ra7 ({After games like
this, black sought new ways of countering the bishop sac. In the post-mortem
afterwards Nigel suggested} 12... Ra4 {and this is now the main line in this
variation} 13. Nbc7+ Kd7 14. O-O Rxe4 {Vitolinsh,A-Sturua,Z/URS Soviet Union
1978/0-1}) ({but Nigel has had success with} 12... Qa5+ 13. c3 Qa4 {e.g. Berg,
K-Povah,N/Wijk aan Zee 1979/0-1.}) 13. Nxa7 Nxa7 14. exf5 Bh6 $6 (14... Bxf5
15. Qf3 Be6 16. Nf6+ Ke7 17. O-O $16 {Emerson,R-Quinteros,M (2555)/Lloyds Bank
op 01st 1977 (1)/0-1}) 15. O-O Qg5 $2 (15... Nc6 16. f6 Bg5 17. f4 exf4 18.
Qe2+ Ne5 19. Qb5+ Bd7 20. Qa6 {is good for white, but at least not losing
immediately}) 16. f4 exf4 17. Qd4 Rg8 18. Nf6+ 1-0

