Premature.} 20. c3 $142) 20... Nc5 21. Rf2 h5 22. Kg2 hxg4 23. hxg4 Ke7 24. Kg3
Rh7 25. Rh2 Rxh2 26. Kxh2 Rh8+ 27. Kg3 f5 $6 {Black should play passively and
make it difficult for White to find openings for his rook and knight} 28. exf6+
Kxf6 29. Nf3 Nxd3 $2 30. g5+ Kg7 31. cxd3 Rc8 32. Nd4 {From here on, although
Rybka only gives white a slight plus, I think it's a technical win for white.}
b4 33. Re1 Kf7 34. Rh1 Kg7 35. Kf3 a5 36. Ke3 Rc7 37. Kd2 Rc8 38. Rc1 Rxc1 39.
Kxc1 Kf7 (39... Kf7 {Adjudicated a win for white, in view of} 40. Nb3 a4 41.
Nc5 Ke7 42. d4 Kd6 43. a3 bxa3 (43... Bb5 44. axb4 Be8 45. Kb1 Ke7 46. Ka2 Kd6
47. Ka3) 44. bxa3 {followed by K-b2-c3-b4 and N:a4}) 1-0

