{I retired from the LARA open after the first round on Friday evening, being
so tired I couldn't face an early morning start. I went up to St Brides to
watch the county match and got called on as a substitute with nearly an hour
gone on the clock. So I was very pleased with this game!} 1. e4 Nf6 2. e5 Nd5
3. d4 d6 4. Nf3 g6 5. Be2 Bg7 6. O-O O-O 7. Bg5 $6 ({The standard line is} 7.
c4) 7... Nc6 8. exd6 cxd6 9. c4 Nb6 10. Nc3 Bg4 11. c5 $2 (11. Be3 {gets to a
standard position where it's normally white to move!}) 11... dxc5 12. dxc5 Qxd1
13. Rfxd1 Bxc3 14. bxc3 Na4 15. h3 $2 Nxc3 16. hxg4 Nxe2+ 17. Kf1 Nc3 18. Rd7
f6 19. Be3 Rab8 20. Nd4 Ne5 21. Rxe7 Nd5 22. Re6 Nxe3+ 23. fxe3 Nxg4 24. Rb1
Rfc8 25. Rb5 a6 26. Ra5 Re8 27. c6 Rxe6 28. Nxe6 bxc6 29. Rxa6 Rb2 30. e4 Ne3+
31. Kg1 Rxg2+ 32. Kh1 Rc2 33. a4 g5 34. a5 g4 35. Ra7 h5 36. Rg7+ Kh8 37. Rg6
h4 38. Rh6+ Kg8 39. Rxh4 g3 0-1

