1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 Nf6 4. dxe5 Nxe4 5. Qd5 Nc5 6. Be3 ({Theory is} 6. Bg5
Be7 7. exd6 Qxd6 8. Nc3 c6 9. Qxd6 Bxd6 10. O-O-O Bc7 11. Bc4 $14 {Karaklajic,
N (2380)-Trifunovic,D/Wch Seniors 05th 1995 (9)/1-0}) 6... Be6 7. Qd4 Nc6 8.
Bb5 Bd7 9. Qc3 Ne6 10. Bxc6 Bxc6 11. Nbd2 Be7 12. O-O-O O-O 13. Nd4 Nxd4 14.
Bxd4 dxe5 15. Bxe5 Bf6 16. Bxf6 Qxf6 17. Qxf6 gxf6 18. Nc4 $14 {White has a
slight advantage, arising from black's shattered pawn structure on the king's
side and the fact that knight and rook can operate well against rook and
bishop.} Rad8 19. Ne3 (19. Na5 Rxd1+ 20. Rxd1 Re8 21. Nxc6 bxc6 22. Kd2 {
weakens black's pawn structure further, but I wanted to keep R+N v R+B.}) 19...
Rd7 20. Rxd7 Bxd7 21. Rd1 Be6 22. Rd4 Re8 23. b3 Re7 24. c4 c6 25. Kc2 Rd7 26.
Kc3 {Now with d6 weakened, it's OK for white to exchange rooks.} Rxd4 27. Kxd4
Kf8 28. f4 Ke7 29. c5 b5 30. f5 Bd7 {White's plan now is to fix the Q-side
pawns, then move K to h5 to force h6, then exchange king's side pawns to gain
an entry at e5.} 31. b4 Bc8 32. Ke4 Bd7 33. Kf4 Kf8 34. Kg4 Kg7 35. Kh5 Bc8 36.
g4 Bd7 37. Nd1 Be8 38. Nc3 Bd7 39. Ne4 Be8 40. Nd6 Bd7 41. a3 a6 42. h3 {
Zugzwang - Black is forced into ...} h6 {Now the white king retraces steps to
f4 and prepares g5.} 43. Kh4 Kf8 44. Kg3 Kg7 45. Kf4 Kf8 46. Ne4 Kg7 47. h4 Be8
48. g5 fxg5+ 49. hxg5 hxg5+ 50. Kxg5 Bd7 51. f6+ Kf8 {In the final phase the
king penetrates to d6.} 52. Kf4 Be6 53. Ke5 Ke8 54. Kd6 Bd5 55. Nf2 Kd8 56. Nd3
{Black resigned. His QBP will fall.} 1-0

