[2]/1-0}) 6... Qxd1+ 7. Kxd1 Bg4 8. Bf4 Nge7 9. Kc2 Nd5 $5 ({Chandler v
Emerson went} 9... O-O-O 10. Bd3 Nd5 $15 {although I eventually lost.}) 10. Bg3
Bf5+ 11. Kc1 g6 12. Nbd2 Bh6 13. h4 O-O 14. Ng5 Rae8 15. f4 Rc8 16. Nc4 f6 17.
exf6 Rxf6 18. Ne5 Nxe5 19. fxe5 Rff8 20. b3 {Hereabouts white starts going
wrong. He was clearly looking to move his king and free the queen's rook} ({on
} 20. Bc4 {I was planning} Be6 21. Rd1 Rcd8 22. Rd2 Bxg5 23. hxg5 Rf5 {but
maybe something like b6 is stronger. White's king's side pawns are weak.})
20... Be6 21. Bd3 Bxg5+ 22. hxg5 Nxc3 23. Kb2 c4 $1 24. Bxc4 Bxc4 25. Kxc3 Be6+
26. Kb2 Rf5 27. Rhf1 $2 (27. Bh4) 27... Rxg5 28. Rf3 Bf5 29. Rc1 Rxc1 30. Kxc1
h5 31. Kd2 Be4 32. Re3 Bd5 33. Rd3 Kf7 34. Ke2 Ke6 35. Bf2 Rxg2 36. Kf1 a6 37.
a4 (37. a4 {adjudicated. Even with opposite colour bishops, it's a win for
black.} g5 38. Rg3 Rxg3 39. Bxg3 h4 40. Be1 Bxb3 41. a5 Kxe5) 0-1

