{I played this game on the Friday evening, completely drunk after a long
session at Balls Brothers to recruit Belinda Bridgen to the tax department. In
the circumstances I think this was a masterpiece! A pity I never got to play
my planned improvement on Fischer's play in the 1970 Olympiad. Nobody ever
played this line against my Grunfeld again.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4.
cxd5 Nxd5 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 Bg7 7. Bc4 O-O 8. Ne2 c5 9. Be3 Nc6 10. O-O Qc7
11. Rc1 Rd8 12. h3 ({Modern theory prefers} 12. Bf4 {in response to which} Be5
$5 {Cheparinov,I (2696)-Ivanchuk,V (2786)/Cap d'Agde CCAS Gp-A rapid 2008 (4)/
0-1 is interesting.}) ({or} 12. Qd2 b6 13. Bh6 {Ponomariov,R (2739)-Aronian,L 
(2786)/Moscow Tal Memorial 4th 2009 (2)/1/2-1/2}) 12... Na5 (12... b6 13. f4 e6
14. Qe1 Na5 15. Bd3 f5 16. g4 {Spassky,B-Fischer,R/Siegen ol (Men) fin-A 1970 
(6)/1-0 is the famous game}) 13. Bd3 b6 14. f4 e6 (14... f5 {has a good score
in practice (from a limited number of lower strength games) but it doesn't
look right to me} 15. exf5 gxf5 {Muender,M (2280)-Stelting,T/Hamburg HSG/BUE
1986/0-1} 16. Ng3 e6 17. Qe2 $14) 15. f5 ({If} 15. Qe1 {I was intending} Bb7
$146 (15... f5 16. g4 {would transpose into Spassky,B-Fischer,R/Siegen ol (Men)
fin-A 1970 (6)/1-0}) 16. g4 Qe7 {to avoid what I see as the weakening ....f5})
15... exf5 16. exf5 Bb7 17. Qe1 $6 ({The start of a faulty plan.} 17. Bg5 Re8
18. f6 Qd7 $11) 17... Re8 (17... Qe7 {may be more precise to stop} 18. Bg5) ({
In any event my move is better than} 17... Qc6 18. Qg3 {Wilen,E-Koskinen,V/
Helsinki op2 2001 (4)/1-0}) 18. Qf2 $2 c4 19. Bb1 Qe7 20. f6 Qxe3 21. fxg7
Qxf2+ ({Even stronger is} 21... Bxg2 $1 22. Kxg2 Qxe2) 22. Rxf2 Re7 23. Nf4
Rae8 24. Bc2 Kxg7 25. Ba4 Re1+ 26. Rf1 Rxf1+ 27. Kxf1 Re4 28. g3 $2 (28. Ne2
Bc6 29. Bd1 Nb7 $17) 28... Re3 29. Ne2 Bf3 30. Ng1 Bd5 31. Kf2 Rd3 32. Ne2 g5
33. Bc2 Rf3+ 34. Kg1 Nb7 35. Rf1 Nd6 36. Rxf3 Bxf3 37. Kf2 Bxe2 38. Kxe2 f5 39.
Ke3 Kf6 40. h4 h6 41. hxg5+ hxg5 42. Kf3 Nb5 0-1

