{Played on the Saturday morning, with a huge hangover from Friday's mammoth
session at the wine bar to recruit Belinda Bridgen to the tax department} 1. e4
c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Bg5 e6 7. f4 b5 8. e5 dxe5 9.
fxe5 Qc7 10. Qe2 Nfd7 11. O-O-O Bb7 12. Qg4 Qxe5 13. Bxb5 {All established
theory. At the time the text was the most popular, but now 13. Be2 seems to
have overtaken it.} axb5 14. Rhe1 h5 15. Qh4 Qc5 16. Qg3 {This and the next
two moves are a suggestion of John Nunn.} Bc6 ({if} 16... Na6 17. Nxe6 fxe6 18.
Rxe6+ Kf7 19. Rxd7+ Kxe6 20. Rxb7 Bd6 21. Bf4 $1 (21. Qh3+ Qf5 22. Qe3+ Qe5 {
Nunn,J (2375)-Stean,M (2370)/Hastings 7576 1975 (9)/ 1/2-1/2}) 21... Nc7 22.
Bxd6 Qxd6 23. Rb6 $1 {Stean,M (2420)-Ungureanu,E (2350) /Netanya 13th 1976 (7)/
1-0}) ({for} 16... h4 17. Qg4 {see my game against J.J. Ady}) 17. h4 $5 Na6 18.
Qd3 Nb4 $2 ({Rybka reckons that best is} 18... Nf6 19. Nxe6 fxe6 20. Qg6+ Ke7
21. Rf1 Qe5 22. Bf4 Qc5 23. Bg5 {with a draw by repetition.}) 19. Qh3 (19.
Rxe6+ $1 {is even stronger}) 19... Nxa2+ $2 (19... Nf6 20. Nxe6 fxe6 21. Qxe6+
Be7 22. Bxf6 gxf6 23. Rd6 Ra7 24. Qxf6 Rg8 25. a3) 20. Nxa2 Rxa2 21. Rxe6+ $1
fxe6 (21... Be7 22. Rxe7+ Kf8 23. Rxf7+ Kxf7 24. Qe6+ Kf8 25. Rf1+ Nf6 26.
Rxf6+ gxf6 27. Qxf6+ Ke8 28. Qxh8+ Qf8 29. Qe5+ Kd7 30. Qe6+ Kc7 31. Qxc6+) 22.
Qxe6+ Be7 23. Qg6+ Kd8 24. Bxe7+ $1 Kxe7 25. Qxg7+ Kd6 ({Now it's mate in 6,
but} 25... Ke8 26. Re1+ Kd8 27. Ne6+ Kc8 28. Qxh8+ Kb7 29. Nxc5+ $18 {is a
total win for white anyway.}) 26. Nxb5+ Ke6 27. Nc7+ Kf5 28. Qg5+ Ke4 29. Re1+
(29. Re1+ Kd4 30. Qe3+ Kc4 31. Qc3#) 1-0

