{This was the last round. I just needed to draw to get first place, having
beaten Craig Pritchett in the previous round.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4.
e4 d6 5. Be2 O-O 6. Nf3 e5 7. O-O Nc6 8. d5 Ne7 9. b4 Nh5 10. c5 Nf4 11. Bxf4
exf4 12. Rc1 f5 $6 (12... a5 {Kamsky,G (2695)-Kasparov,G (2815)/PCA/Intel-GP
rapid 1994 (1)/0-1 or}) (12... h6 {Goodman,D-Duer,A/Wch U20 Innsbruck 1977 (13)
/0-1 is better. The text was given as a main line in MCO, without mentioning
David Goodman's reply.}) 13. e5 $1 $146 dxe5 14. d6 cxd6 15. cxd6 Nc6 16. Qd5+
Kh8 17. b5 Nd4 18. Nxe5 Be6 $2 (18... Qe8 $1 19. Qxd4 {Johansson,V (2155)
-Rajcsanyi,Z (2145)/Wch U20 Girls 1992/1/2-1/2} Qxe5 20. Qxe5 Bxe5 21. Rfd1 Rd8
$11) 19. Qxd4 Qf6 20. Nxg6+ hxg6 21. Qxf4 Rad8 22. Rfd1 Qe5 23. Qh4+ Kg8 24.
Bc4 $16 Bf6 25. Bxe6+ Qxe6 26. Qb4 Be5 27. Qc5 Bxd6 28. Qxa7 Qe5 29. g3 Bc5 30.
Qa4 Rd4 31. Rxd4 Bxd4 32. Qc4+ Kg7 33. Ne2 Bb6 34. Qc3 Qxc3 35. Rxc3 Rd8 36.
Rc2 Rd5 37. a4 Rd1+ 38. Kg2 Ra1 39. Rc4 Ra2 40. Kf3 g5 41. Nd4 Kf6 42. Nc2 Ke5
43. Ke2 $2 Rb2 44. f4+ gxf4 45. gxf4+ Kd5 {Now white only has a slight
advantage...} 46. Rc8 Ra2 47. Kd3 Rxa4 48. Rb8 Rxf4 {which has now disappeared.
} 49. Rxb7 Rf3+ {Now we'd reached the time control, we agreed a draw.} 1/2-1/2

