1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 e6 6. Ndb5 d6 7. Bf4 e5 8.
Bg5 a6 9. Na3 b5 10. Bxf6 gxf6 11. Nd5 f5 12. exf5 Bxf5 13. c3 Bg7 14. Nc2 O-O
15. Nce3 Be6 16. Qh5 $146 ({This was prepared especially by the Mushrooms
players Linton, Harris and Pelling for use against Streatham & Brixton.} 16. g4
{was the main move at the time, but} Qh4 17. Bg2 e4 {is very dangerous,
despite Rybka's assessment of advantage to white e.g. Dementiev,O-Majorovas,V/
URS Soviet Union 1977/0-1}) 16... f5 17. Bd3 {There are now over 600 games on
the database with this position} e4 18. Bc2 Ne7 19. Nf4 ({The main line now is
} 19. Rd1 b4 20. O-O (20. Nxb4 a5 21. Nbd5 Nxd5 22. Nxd5 Rb8 23. Bb3 a4 24.
Bxa4 Rxb2 25. Bb3 {Fressinet,L (2595)-Gelfand,B (2700)/Enghien les Bains 2003 
(4)/0-1}) 20... bxc3 $11 {Ponomariov,R (2684)-Leko,P (2739)/WchT 5th Yerevan
2001 (5.1)/1/2-1/2}) 19... Bf7 20. Qg5 ({Losing control of d5. He played this
after some thought, reckoning on his 22nd move to gain the advantage} 20. Bb3
$142 d5 21. Qg5 b4 (21... Ng6 22. Qxd8 Raxd8 {Anand,V (2769)-Kramnik,V (2758)/
Fujitsu Siemens Giants rapid 2000 (5)/1/2-1/2}) 22. O-O (22. cxb4 Kh8 23. O-O
d4 24. Bxf7 Rxf7 25. Nc4 d3 $13) 22... bxc3 23. bxc3 h6 {Zontakh,A (2576)
-Komarov,D (2568)/Niksic 2000/1/2-1/2}) 20... Ng6 21. Qxf5 $2 (21. Qxd8 Raxd8
22. Nxg6 hxg6 $17 {Harris,R/Povah,N from the same match as this}) 21... Bc4 $1
22. Ne6 Bxc3+ $1 23. Kd1 ({if} 23. bxc3 Qa5 24. Nxf8 Qxc3+ 25. Kd1 Qxa1+ 26.
Kd2 Qd4+ 27. Kc1 Rxf8 28. Qxe4 Qa1+ 29. Bb1 Bxa2 $19) 23... Rxf5 24. Nxd8 Rxf2
({or} 24... Bxb2 25. Nxf5 Bxa1 26. Nc6 d5 $19) 25. bxc3 Rxd8 26. Nxc4 bxc4 27.
Bxe4 d5 28. Ke1 Rb2 29. Rb1 Rxa2 30. Bxg6 hxg6 31. Rf1 Re8+ 32. Kd1 d4 {
and white resigned. One of my best games I think.} 0-1

