1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. exd5 exd5 5. Qf3 $6 {played to get out of main
line theory} Nc6 (5... Qe7+ 6. Be2 Nc6 {Galego,L (2390) -Santos,A (2285)/
Lisbon m 1993 (4)/1-0 is perhaps even stronger}) 6. Bb5 Nge7 7. Nge2 Bf5 8. Ba4
O-O 9. O-O Bxc3 10. Qxc3 Nb8 $6 {very slow. White gets a slight bind on.} 11.
Ng3 Bg6 12. Bf4 c6 13. Rfe1 Nf5 14. Nxf5 Bxf5 15. Bb3 Qd7 16. Qg3 Na6 17. a3
Rfe8 18. f3 Kh8 19. Rxe8+ Rxe8 20. Re1 Rxe1+ 21. Qxe1 {Houdini assesses this
position as equal! Material may be level, but the point is that black's
queen's knight can't get into the game.} Be6 22. Qe5 f6 23. Qd6 Qxd6 $2 ({
He should have kept the queens on with} 23... Qe8 {although after} 24. Bd2 {
white still has the advantage}) 24. Bxd6 Kg8 25. c3 Kf7 26. Bc2 g6 27. f4 Bd7
28. f5 $1 gxf5 (28... Bxf5 29. Bxf5 gxf5 30. Kf2 Ke6 31. Bf4 Kd7 32. Kg3 c5 33.
Kh4 Kc6 34. Kh5 Kb5 35. Kh6 cxd4 36. Kxh7 dxc3 (36... Kc4 37. Kg6 d3 38. h4 Nc7
39. Kxf6 {is winning}) 37. bxc3 Nc5 38. h4 Ne6 39. Bd2 {is winning}) 29. Kf2
Ke6 30. Bf4 b5 {adjudicated win for white} (30... b5 31. b4 Be8 32. a4 (32. Bd3
Bg6 33. a4 bxa4 34. Bxa6 a3 35. Bc1 a2 36. Bb2) 32... Bh5 (32... bxa4 33. Bxa4
Ke7 (33... Kd7 34. b5 Nc7 35. bxc6+ Kc8 36. Bd6 h6 37. Ke3 Ne6 38. g3 Nd8 39.
Bc2 Nxc6 40. Bxf5+ Bd7 41. Bd3) 34. Bc2 Kd8 35. Bd3 Nc7 36. Bxc7+ Kxc7 37. Ke3
Kb6 38. Bxf5 h6) 33. axb5 cxb5 34. g4 fxg4 (34... Bxg4 35. Bd3 {wins the knight
}) 35. Bxh7 Kd7 36. Bf5+ Kd8 37. Kg3 Nc7 38. Bxc7+ Kxc7 39. Bxg4 Bg6 40. h4 Bc2
41. Kf4 Kd6 42. h5 Ke7 43. Bf5 {wins. White has an outside passed pawn and all
black's pawms are vulnerable.}) 1-0

