1. Nf3 Nf6 2. g3 g6 3. b4 Bg7 4. Bb2 O-O 5. c4 c6 6. Na3 $6 (6. Bg2 a5 7. b5
cxb5 8. cxb5 a4 {Keene, R-Jakobsen,O/WchT U26 fin-A 13th 1966 (3)/1/2-1/2})
6... Qb6 7. Qb3 a5 8. b5 d5 ({Rybka likes} 8... Ne4 9. e3 a4 10. Qc2 Bxb2 11.
Qxb2 d6 $15) 9. cxd5 cxd5 10. Bg2 Nbd7 11. d4 Qd6 12. O-O Nb6 13. Ne5 Bf5 14.
Rac1 a4 15. Qe3 Nfd7 16. Nb1 Bxb1 17. Rxb1 a3 18. Bc3 Ra4 19. Rfc1 Nc4 20. Nxc4
Rxc4 21. Rb3 ({Rybka suggests} 21. Qd2 Rfc8 22. e3 {to organise knocking the
rook out of c4. It analyses this to a draw after} Qc7 23. Rb3 e5 24. Bxd5 exd4
25. Bxc4 dxc3 26. Rbxc3 Bxc3 27. Rxc3 Nb6 28. Bxf7+ Qxf7 29. Rxc8+ Nxc8 30.
Qd8+ Qf8 31. Qd5+ Qf7) 21... Rfc8 22. Rcb1 e6 23. Bb4 Qb6 24. Bc5 Nxc5 25. dxc5
R4xc5 26. Rxa3 Bd4 $1 27. Qf4 e5 28. Qf3 e4 29. Qf4 Rxb5 (29... Rc2 $142 30.
Bf1 Qe6 31. Rd1 Bc5 $17) 30. Rab3 Rxb3 31. Rxb3 Qc6 32. e3 Bg7 33. Bf1 h5 {
Now White's queen doesn't have many safe squares.} 34. Bb5 Qe6 35. Kg2 Bf6 $2 (
35... Rc2 36. Rb1 Be5 37. Qg5 Bf6 38. Qf4 Kg7 39. Ba4 Rxa2 40. Bb3 Re2 41. Rd1
g5 42. Qc7 Qf5 {wins}) 36. h4 $2 (36. Bd7 $1 {takes away most of black's
advantage.}) 36... Kg7 37. a4 Be7 ({More accurate is} 37... Bd8 38. Be8 Qxe8
39. Qd6 Qc6 40. Qb4 Qf6) 38. Be8 Rxe8 39. Qc7 Rc8 40. Qxb7 Qf5 (40... Qf5 41.
Rb1 Qf3+ 42. Kg1 Rc2 43. Rf1 Bd6 {and the threat of Bg3 and subsequent mate
can't be stopped.}) 0-1

