{Half a point ahead of the field, a win would enable me to win the tournament.
} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. g4 a6 7. g5 Nfd7 8.
Be3 b5 9. a3 Nb6 10. h4 N8d7 11. h5 Bb7 12. Rh3 ({My innovation against
Pritchett, but maybe even stronger is} 12. g6 $1 hxg6 13. hxg6 Rxh1 14. gxf7+
Kxf7 15. Qf3+ Qf6 16. Qxh1 {Adams,M (2600)-Hansen,C (2565)/ Hoogovens Wijk aan
Zee 1991 (7)/1-0}) 12... Nc5 13. g6 hxg6 (13... Qe7 14. gxf7+ Qxf7 15. Qg4 {
was my game against Pritchett and Idelstein,M (2300)-Barash,D (2240)/Israel
1987/1-0}) 14. hxg6 Rxh3 15. gxf7+ Kxf7 16. Bxh3 Nc4 17. Qh5+ g6 18. Qh7+ Bg7
19. Nxe6 ({More accurate is} 19. Bxe6+ Nxe6 20. Nxe6 Kxe6 21. Qxg7 Nxe3) (19.
b4 {(Jon Levitt)} Qh8 $1 20. Qxh8 Rxh8 21. Bg2 (21. bxc5 Rxh3 22. c6 Bxc6)
21... Na4) 19... Nxe6 20. Bxe6+ Kxe6 21. Qxg7 Nxe3 22. Qxg6+ ({Rybka likes} 22.
Ke2 $1 Ng4 23. Qxb7 Qh4 24. Qd5+ Ke7 25. Qd4 $16 {but the game continuation is
easier on the nerves!}) (22. Ne2 {(Smerdon!)} Nxc2+ 23. Kd2 Bxe4) 22... Qf6 23.
Qxf6+ Kxf6 24. fxe3 Ke5 25. O-O-O Bxe4 26. Nxe4 Kxe4 27. Rxd6 Kxe3 {Dave
Rumens thought this was a draw, because it's 3 v 2 without a passed pawn (see
Fine p372). But actually it's a win for White because Black's king is cut off
and White can reach the Lucena position - see Fine p291.} 28. b4 Ke4 29. Kb2
Ke5 30. Rb6 Kd5 31. Kb3 Ra7 32. a4 bxa4+ 33. Kxa4 Ra8 34. Ka5 Rc8 35. Kxa6 Rxc2
36. Rb7 Ra2+ 37. Kb6 Kd6 38. b5 Ra1 39. Rb8 Kd7 40. Kb7 Rh1 41. Rc8 Rb1 42.
Rc7+ Kd6 43. b6 Rb2 44. Rc1 Rh2 45. Ka7 Ra2+ 46. Kb8 {We've got to the Lucena
position, so Black resigned.} 1-0

