{First game of the 1979-80 season, with a new grade of 208, published in CHESS
in September 1979 p362.} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 a6 5. Bd3 Nc6 6.
Nxc6 dxc6 7. f4 ({Premature. Better is first} 7. O-O) 7... e5 8. f5 Nf6 9. Qf3
b5 10. a4 Bb7 11. Be3 Bb4+ 12. Ke2 $6 ({better} 12. Kf2 O-O 13. Rd1) ({or} 12.
Nd2 O-O 13. g4 c5 14. g5) 12... Qe7 13. c3 Bc5 14. Bg5 $6 h6 15. Bh4 Rd8 16.
Nd2 Bb6 17. Rhd1 O-O 18. Bc2 Rd6 19. g4 $6 (19. a5 Bc7 20. Nb3 c5 21. Qg3 c4
22. Nc5 $15) 19... g5 20. Bg3 Rfd8 $15 21. a5 Ba7 22. Nb3 Rxd1 23. Rxd1 Rxd1
24. Kxd1 c5 25. Bf2 $2 c4 $1 26. Bxa7 cxb3 27. Bxb3 Bxe4 28. Qe3 Bf3+ ({
Rybka prefers} 28... Qd8+ 29. Ke2 Qxa5 30. Bb8 Qa1 31. Bxe5 Qxb2+ 32. Ke1 Qb1+
33. Kd2 Qxb3 34. Bxf6 Qc2+ {but it's still not straightforward for black to
win.}) 29. Kc1 Bxg4 30. Bc5 Qb7 31. Qxe5 Qh1+ 32. Kd2 Qg2+ 33. Ke1 Kh7 34. Qe7
Qh1+ 35. Kf2 Qxh2+ 36. Ke1 Bh5 (36... Qh1+ 37. Kf2 Qf3+ 38. Ke1 Qe4+ 39. Qxe4
Nxe4 40. Be7 Bxf5 41. Bxf7 {was the last chance of retaining an advantage, but
white's two bishops make it difficult for black to make meaningful progress.})
37. Bxf7 Qh1+ 38. Kf2 {Draw agreed on adjournment. Black doesn't have better
than perpetual check.} 1/2-1/2

